  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:march_stone_bricks",
      "title": "Building with the March",
      "text": [
        "March stone, cobble and planks make a full building set. Four March Stone in a square give **March Stone Bricks**; four bricks give **Polished March Stone**; two brick slabs stacked give **Chiseled March Stone Bricks**, carved with a drum and a teal eye.",
        "Every stone has **stairs** and **slabs**, and all but polished stone have **walls**. The Stonecutter turns plain March Stone into any of them with no waste.",
        "**Moonstone** and **Moss Agate** build the same way: four in a square give their bricks, four bricks give the polished stone, and the Stonecutter turns the plain stone into any of its set.",
        "**Pale Stone**, **Frost Shale**, **Ochre Sandstone**, **Salt Crust** and the four **Kiln Clays** have stairs, slabs and walls too, crafted the usual way or cut on the Stonecutter.",
        "Two of a stone in a row give its **pressure plate**, and players and mobs can stand on it. One stone gives its **button**, which stays on for a second.",
        "Smelting **March Stone Bricks**, **Moonstone Bricks** or **Moss Agate Bricks** cracks them. Two **Moonstone Brick Slabs** stacked give **Chiseled Moonstone Bricks**, and two **Moss Agate Brick Slabs** stacked give **Chiseled Moss Agate Bricks**. The Stonecutter cuts those too."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:march_door",
      "title": "March wood",
      "text": [
        "March Planks work like any other wood: stairs, slabs, a fence and a fence gate, a door with lit window slits, a trapdoor, a pressure plate and a button. The usual recipes apply, and they burn like other wood."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Double doors",
      "text": [
        "Tribal Power's doors open in pairs. Set two side by side, facing the same way, and opening one swings its twin with it.",
        "Hold **sneak** when you click to move just the one."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
